.TH C-ARBINT 3 "@MAN_DATE@" "c-arbint @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
c-arbint \- portable arbitrary-precision integer library for C
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <arbint.h>
.fi
.PP
Link with:
.PP
.nf
.B cc ... $(pkg-config --cflags --libs c-arbint)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B c-arbint
provides signed arbitrary-precision integer arithmetic with explicit
allocator-aware object management and runtime performance optimization.
.PP
This page documents the functions currently exported by
.BR libarbint
(version 0.0.1).
Additional declarations may exist in
.BR arbint.h
for future releases.
.PP
The library includes optimized code paths for x86 processors supporting
BMI2 (multiplication) and AVX2 (doubling) instructions, with automatic
runtime dispatch based on CPU feature detection.
.SH TYPES
.TP
.B arbint_t
Opaque integer object type (single-object array form). Initialize with
.BR arbint_init ()
and release with
.BR arbint_clear ().
.TP
.B arbint_ctx_t
Execution/allocation context. A context carries the allocator used for object
storage and for exported buffers.
.TP
.B arbint_err_t
Error code enum used by mutating/extracting APIs.
.TP
.B arbint_rng_t
Mersenne Twister (MT19937) PRNG state. Initialize with
.BR arbint_rng_init ()
and release with
.BR arbint_rng_clear ().
.SH RETURN VALUES
.PP
Functions returning
.B arbint_err_t
use
.B ARBINT_OK
on success and a nonzero error code on failure.
.PP
Predicate/comparison helpers return
.B int
(typically boolean-style 0/1 or three-way compare \-1/0/+1).
.SH ERROR CODES
.TP
.B ARBINT_EINVAL
Invalid argument (for example NULL where not accepted, or invalid object state).
.TP
.B ARBINT_ENOMEM
Allocation failure.
.TP
.B ARBINT_EOVERFLOW
Value/capacity overflow for the requested conversion or operation.
.TP
.B ARBINT_ESIGN
Unsigned extraction requested from a negative value.
.TP
.B ARBINT_EDOM
Domain error (e.g.\& platform entropy source failed, or
.BR arbint_urandomm ()
bound is not positive).
.TP
.B ARBINT_EZERO
Division by zero.
.SH IMPLEMENTED API
.SS Context and Object Lifetime
.BR arbint_ctx_init_default (),
.BR arbint_ctx_init (),
.BR arbint_ctx_clear (),
.BR arbint_init (),
.BR arbint_init_all (),
.BR arbint_clear (),
.BR arbint_clear_all (),
.BR arbint_get_ctx (),
.BR arbint_set_ctx (),
.BR arbint_zero (),
.BR arbint_resize (),
.BR arbint_swap ()
.PP
These APIs initialize/destroy contexts and integer objects, rebind objects to a
new context, zero values, reserve limb capacity, and swap complete object state.
.PP
.BI "arbint_err_t arbint_init_all(arbint_ctx_t *" ctx ", arbint_t " a ", ...)"
.RS
Initialize a NULL-terminated list of
.B arbint_t
values with the same context. If any initialization fails, all previously
initialized values in the list are cleared and the error is returned.
The argument list must be terminated with a
.B (arbint_t *) NULL
sentinel.
.RE
.PP
.BI "void arbint_clear_all(arbint_t " a ", ...)"
.RS
Clear a NULL-terminated list of
.B arbint_t
values. Each value is passed to
.BR arbint_clear ().
The argument list must be terminated with a
.B (arbint_t *) NULL
sentinel.
.RE
.SS Assignment and Extraction
.BR arbint_set (),
.BR arbint_set_i32 (),
.BR arbint_set_u32 (),
.BR arbint_get_i32 (),
.BR arbint_get_u32 ()
.PP
Assign from another integer or a 32-bit scalar; extract into 32-bit scalar
forms with range/sign checking.
.SS Fit Checks
.BR arbint_fits_u8 (),
.BR arbint_fits_u16 (),
.BR arbint_fits_u32 (),
.BR arbint_fits_u64 (),
.BR arbint_fits_i8 (),
.BR arbint_fits_i16 (),
.BR arbint_fits_i32 (),
.BR arbint_fits_i64 ()
.PP
Non-allocating representability predicates.
.SS Sign and Basic Predicates
.BR arbint_signum (),
.BR arbint_is_zero (),
.BR arbint_is_one (),
.BR arbint_is_neg (),
.BR arbint_is_odd (),
.BR arbint_is_even (),
.BR arbint_abs (),
.BR arbint_neg ()
.PP
Sign/shape queries and sign transforms.
.SS Comparison
.BR arbint_cmp (),
.BR arbint_cmpabs (),
.BR arbint_cmp_i32 (),
.BR arbint_cmp_u32 (),
.BR arbint_eq (),
.BR arbint_ne (),
.BR arbint_lt (),
.BR arbint_le (),
.BR arbint_gt (),
.BR arbint_ge (),
.BR arbint_eq_i32 (),
.BR arbint_ne_i32 (),
.BR arbint_lt_i32 (),
.BR arbint_le_i32 (),
.BR arbint_gt_i32 (),
.BR arbint_ge_i32 (),
.BR arbint_eq_u32 (),
.BR arbint_ne_u32 (),
.BR arbint_lt_u32 (),
.BR arbint_le_u32 (),
.BR arbint_gt_u32 (),
.BR arbint_ge_u32 ()
.PP
Three-way and predicate comparisons against big integers and 32-bit scalars.
.SS Arithmetic
.BR arbint_add (),
.BR arbint_sub (),
.BR arbint_mul (),
.BR arbint_sqr (),
.BR arbint_add_i32 (),
.BR arbint_add_u32 (),
.BR arbint_sub_i32 (),
.BR arbint_sub_u32 (),
.BR arbint_mul_i32 (),
.BR arbint_mul_u32 ()
.PP
Core signed arithmetic on arbitrary-size integers.
Scalar multiplication variants
.RB ( arbint_mul_i32 ", " arbint_mul_u32 )
provide optimized fast paths for multiplication by 32-bit values with
early-exit for special cases (0, ±1).
.SS Truncated Division and Remainder
.BR arbint_tdiv_qr (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_q (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_r (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_qr_u32 (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_q_u32 (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_r_u32 (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_qr_i32 (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_q_i32 (),
.BR arbint_tdiv_r_i32 ()
.PP
Truncated division obeys:
.PP
.nf
q = trunc(n / d)
r = n - q*d
.fi
.PP
with
.I |r| < |d|
and remainder sign matching the dividend (or zero).
.SS Binary Import and Export
.BR arbint_import (),
.BR arbint_export ()
.PP
Convert between
.B arbint_t
and a little-endian magnitude byte buffer.
.B arbint_export ()
exports magnitude only (no sign encoding).
.SS Random Number Generation
.BR arbint_rng_init (),
.BR arbint_rng_clear (),
.BR arbint_urandomb (),
.BR arbint_urandomm ()
.PP
.BI "arbint_err_t arbint_rng_init(arbint_rng_t *" rng ", const void *" seed ", size_t " seed_len ")"
.RS
Initialize an MT19937 PRNG state. If
.I seed
is NULL, the state is seeded from a platform entropy source (see
.B ENTROPY SOURCES
below). If
.I seed
is non-NULL, it must point to a buffer of
.I seed_len
bytes, where
.I seed_len
is a positive multiple of 4.
Returns
.B ARBINT_EINVAL
if no platform entropy source is available (when
.I seed
is NULL) or if
.I seed_len
is invalid.
Returns
.B ARBINT_EDOM
if the platform entropy source fails at runtime.
.RE
.PP
.BI "void arbint_rng_clear(arbint_rng_t *" rng ")"
.RS
Securely zero the PRNG state to prevent leaking generated sequences.
.RE
.PP
.BI "arbint_err_t arbint_urandomb(arbint_t " rop ", arbint_rng_t *" rng ", size_t " k ")"
.RS
Set
.I rop
to a uniformly random non-negative integer in [0,\ 2^\fIk\fP).
.RE
.PP
.BI "arbint_err_t arbint_urandomm(arbint_t " rop ", arbint_rng_t *" rng ", const arbint_t " bound ")"
.RS
Set
.I rop
to a uniformly random non-negative integer in [0,\ \fIbound\fP).
Uses rejection sampling to eliminate modulo bias.
.I rop
may alias
.IR bound .
Returns
.B ARBINT_EDOM
if
.I bound
\(<= 0 or if rejection sampling exhausts 256 attempts.
.RE
.SH ALIASING RULES
.PP
For single-output operations, destination may alias an input.
.PP
For two-output division APIs, output aliases are accepted; if both outputs are
the same object, the last-written output value remains in that object.
.SH MEMORY NOTES
.PP
.B arbint_export ()
allocates the output buffer using the allocator in the source object's context.
The caller owns that buffer and must free it with the same allocator contract.
.SH ALGORITHMIC NOTES
.PP
.B Multiplication
dispatches between a generic implementation and an optimized
BMI2 path on supported x86 targets (using runtime CPU detection).
The implementation switches between schoolbook (O(n²)) and Karatsuba
(O(n^log₂3)) algorithms based on operand size (threshold: 32 limbs).
.PP
.B Division
by multi-limb divisors uses binary long division with magnitude comparison.
Division by single-limb divisors (u32/i32 variants) uses a reciprocal-based
algorithm (Granlund-Montgomery technique) that replaces expensive hardware
DIV instructions with two multiplications per limb plus minimal ALU operations.
This provides significant speedup for the common case of dividing large
integers by small constants.
.PP
.B Doubling
operations automatically select an AVX2-optimized SIMD implementation when
available and operand size exceeds the threshold (16 limbs), providing
1.5-2.5x speedup on modern x86-64 processors.
.PP
All division variants apply appropriate sign rules for truncation semantics
after magnitude computation.
.SH ENTROPY SOURCES
.PP
When
.BR arbint_rng_init ()
is called with a NULL seed, it reads entropy from the best available
platform source. Sources are selected at compile time in the following
priority order:
.PP
.TP
.B Windows
.BR BCryptGenRandom ()
(requires
.IR bcrypt.h ,
Vista+), then
.BR CryptGenRandom ()
(requires
.IR wincrypt.h ,
XP+), then
.B RtlGenRandom
(loaded dynamically from
.IR advapi32.dll ,
XP+; needs only
.IR windows.h ).
.TP
.B macOS/BSD
.BR arc4random_buf ()
(kernel-seeded, cannot fail).
.TP
.B Linux/POSIX
.I /dev/urandom
(opened, read, and closed on each call).
.PP
If no platform entropy source was detected at configure time, or if entropy
support was disabled with
.BR \-\-disable-entropy ,
then NULL-seed initialization returns
.BR ARBINT_EINVAL .
Callers must then supply their own seed buffer.
.SH CONFIGURE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-entropy
Do not compile any platform entropy source.
.BR arbint_rng_init ()
with a NULL seed will always return
.BR ARBINT_EINVAL ;
callers must provide their own seed.
The PRNG itself
.RB ( arbint_urandomb ", " arbint_urandomm )
is unaffected.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <arbint.h>

arbint_ctx_t ctx;
arbint_t a, b, q, r;

arbint_ctx_init_default(&ctx);
arbint_init_all(&ctx, a, b, q, r, (arbint_t *) NULL);

arbint_set_i32(a, -17);
arbint_set_i32(b, 5);
arbint_tdiv_qr(q, r, a, b); /* q = -3, r = -2 */

arbint_clear_all(a, b, q, r, (arbint_t *) NULL);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg-config (1)
